  "name": "COXSACKIE ANTIBODY - IgG",
  "code": "2716",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>The <strong data-start=\"58\" data-end=\"94\">Coxsackievirus IgG antibody test</strong> detects the presence of <strong data-start=\"119\" data-end=\"143\">IgG-class antibodies</strong> to Coxsackievirus, a group of enteroviruses. It is typically used to determine <strong data-start=\"223\" data-end=\"240\">past exposure</strong> or <strong data-start=\"244\" data-end=\"273\">long-term immune response</strong> rather than an active infection.</p>\n<p data-start=\"1383\" data-end=\"1405\"><strong data-start=\"1387\" data-end=\"1405\">Clinical Notes</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1407\" data-end=\"1854\">\n<li data-start=\"1407\" data-end=\"1470\">\n<p data-start=\"1409\" data-end=\"1470\">A <strong data-start=\"1411\" data-end=\"1427\">positive IgG</strong> alone does <strong data-start=\"1439\" data-end=\"1469\">not confirm active disease</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1471\" data-end=\"1564\">\n<p data-start=\"1473\" data-end=\"1564\">Most healthy individuals may have Coxsackie IgG from prior asymptomatic or mild infections.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1565\" data-end=\"1854\">\n<p data-start=\"1567\" data-end=\"1684\">The test may include serotypes from <strong data-start=\"1603\" data-end=\"1626\">group A and group B</strong> Coxsackieviruses, which are linked to various conditions:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1687\" data-end=\"1854\">\n<li data-start=\"1687\" data-end=\"1739\">\n<p data-start=\"1689\" data-end=\"1739\">Group A: hand, foot, and mouth disease, herpangina</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1742\" data-end=\"1854\">\n<p data-start=\"1744\" data-end=\"1854\">Group B: viral myocarditis, pericarditis, pleurodynia, and sometimes implicated in chronic autoimmune diseases</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Result</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Meaning</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Positive IgG</strong></td>\n<td>Indicates <strong>past infection</strong> or <strong>exposure</strong> to Coxsackievirus. The immune system has produced antibodies, which may remain detectable for years.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Negative IgG</strong></td>\n<td>No evidence of past exposure or immunity to Coxsackievirus. The individual may be susceptible to infection.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Rising titers</strong> (on paired samples)</td>\n<td>Suggests a <strong>recent infection</strong> when there&rsquo;s a <strong>fourfold rise</strong> in IgG levels over 2&ndash;3 weeks.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
